==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} ''[[ditie]]'' or ''[[dité]]'', from ''[[ditier]]'', from {{etyl|la}} ''[[dictare|dictāre]]'' (participle ''[[dictatus]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-ditty.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|En-uk-ditty.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪti}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|ditt|ies}}

# A short [[verse]] or [[tune]].
#: ''The Acme mattress '''ditty''' has been stuck in my head all day.''

====Translations====
{{trans-top|a short verse or tune}}
